WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.240
Meet Veri Gate.

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:07.577
Record which vehicle is moving, who is driving, and when it passes through the gate.

3
00:00:07.577 --> 00:00:10.219
Here is the current review workflow.

4
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.957
Start by scanning the vehicle barcode.

5
00:00:13.907 --> 00:00:18.198
The field opens scan ready, with keyboard input suppressed.

6
00:00:18.198 --> 00:00:21.304
When typing is needed, tap the field.

7
00:00:21.304 --> 00:00:24.293
The tap marks that entry as manual.

8
00:00:25.113 --> 00:00:28.298
Next, scan the driver employee number.

9
00:00:28.248 --> 00:00:32.011
Confirm the driver before choosing the movement direction.

10
00:00:32.863 --> 00:00:37.994
Employee numbers can include letters, as this demonstration record shows.

11
00:00:37.944 --> 00:00:46.526
Numeric forms such as one zero zero three and E M P dash one zero zero three still resolve to E one zero zero three.

12
00:00:47.363 --> 00:00:50.612
Choose whether the vehicle is entering or leaving.

13
00:00:50.562 --> 00:00:53.294
Then continue to the review screen.

14
00:00:54.113 --> 00:00:58.329
Choose the direction, then review the movement before submitting.

15
00:00:58.279 --> 00:01:01.823
The scanner returns to the start after recording it.

16
00:01:02.655 --> 00:01:06.806
An unknown scanned barcode continues without a barcode warning.

17
00:01:06.756 --> 00:01:12.426
Its vehicle record is created when the movement is submitted, without a Check barcode flag.

18
00:01:12.426 --> 00:01:15.210
Normal driver checks still apply.

19
00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:19.524
When typing is needed, tap the barcode field.

20
00:01:19.474 --> 00:01:23.366
That tap enables typing and records manual entry.

21
00:01:23.366 --> 00:01:27.476
A partial barcode such as G zero zero is refused.

22
00:01:27.476 --> 00:01:29.796
Enter all four digits.

23
00:01:30.613 --> 00:01:35.834
A complete typed barcode that is not in inventory warns: Check this barcode.

24
00:01:35.784 --> 00:01:38.104
Continue if it is right.

25
00:01:38.104 --> 00:01:43.735
The movement can proceed, and the vehicle is marked Check barcode for supervisor review.

26
00:01:44.572 --> 00:01:52.846
In the console, the vehicle created from the typed unknown barcode is marked Check barcode, making it visible for supervisor review.

27
00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:59.865
For a driver who needs temporary authorization, approval requires a Fleet Lead or higher role.

28
00:01:59.815 --> 00:02:03.642
Here, an approver with the Scanner role is refused.

29
00:02:04.488 --> 00:02:10.405
Choose nine hours, twelve hours, today, forty eight hours, or three days.

30
00:02:10.355 --> 00:02:13.203
Nine hours is the default selection.

31
00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:20.307
The desktop console brings vehicle inventory and operational records together for supervisors.

32
00:02:21.072 --> 00:02:24.346
To add a vehicle, enter its V I N.

33
00:02:24.296 --> 00:02:27.325
Other details can be completed later.

34
00:02:27.325 --> 00:02:32.106
Leave the barcode blank to assign the next free G barcode automatically.

35
00:02:32.947 --> 00:02:38.129
The saved vehicle now appears in inventory with its automatically assigned barcode.

36
00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:41.249
Select its V I N to open the record.

37
00:02:42.072 --> 00:02:48.581
User records open from their User I D or name, keeping the record directly accessible from the list.

38
00:02:49.363 --> 00:02:52.754
Select a Device I D to open that device.

39
00:02:52.704 --> 00:02:58.722
Supervisors can review the location and device details associated with gate operations.

40
00:02:59.572 --> 00:03:04.689
Search movement history by driver, vehicle, location, or date.

41
00:03:04.639 --> 00:03:08.866
The information captured at the gate remains available to review.

42
00:03:09.697 --> 00:03:13.564
This Android review build stores records on the device.

43
00:03:13.514 --> 00:03:18.501
Shared cloud data and automatic synchronization are still being developed.

44
00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:23.463
Veri Gate brings a focused workflow to the gate and a clearer record afterward.
